  "body": "## Problem\nThe current observer can now apply and persist the exact Vinted model filter, but it still re-validates every filtered row with the local title/URL matcher. That turns a valid exact-model catalog (for example Vinted showing hundreds of `iPad 10.9 (2022)` results) into `matched=0`. The UI then keeps Today / This week / Previous full week at zero or unavailable.\n\nThe current scanner also keeps reading the same first catalog batch instead of traversing Vinted's `page=` result pages.\n\n## Changes\n- trust the exact persisted Vinted category + brand + model filter for `VINTED_MODEL`; keep strict local matching for `SEARCH_QUERY`\n- traverse filtered catalog pages while preserving the active Vinted filters, up to the configured safety limit\n- inspect accepted listing detail HTML and read Vinted's own `Dodane ...` publication age / explicit publication date\n- prefer the visible `Dodane` field and fall back to structured publication metadata only when needed\n- store publication timestamps separately in `market_listing_observation.published_at`\n- add a narrow idempotent local schema compatibility initializer for that column/index (Flyway remains untouched)\n- keep a scan incomplete when a required listing publication time could not be resolved, so calendar stats are never silently guessed\n- count Today from 00:00, This week from Monday 00:00, and Previous full week from the previous Monday-Sunday window using the Vinted publication timestamp\n- make those calendar windows available immediately after a complete publication-enriched baseline instead of waiting a week from observer startup\n\n## Scope\nNo changes to normal bot sessions, login/CAPTCHA behavior, negotiation actions, quotas, mobile connectivity, or normal catalog targeting. Publication enrichment is isolated to the anonymous read-only market observer.\n\n## Tests\n- publication parser covers minutes, hours, days and absolute timestamps\n- observation context covers new listings and retrying known rows whose publication time is still missing\n",
